# Binary artifacts: never apply line-ending conversion
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.drawio.png binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Scripts executed INSIDE Linux containers: always LF, on every platform.
# These are COPYed into images (qm sandbox launchers, deer-flow patch tasks);
# a CRLF checkout makes them fail with “env: 'bash\r': No such file or
# directory” at runtime. Found live 2026-10-05 (plan 025, D-2): the published
# sandbox image carries CRLF launchers because trees checked out on
# Windows/macOS fed autocrlf output into the build.
deploy/qm-pacgate/sandbox/tools/** text eol=lf
deploy/qm-pacgate/tasks/** text eol=lf
deploy/qm-pacgate/sandbox/Dockerfile text eol=lf
# The exec-daemon wrapper (2026-10-05): its Dockerfile COPYs
# microvm-agent.mjs into the wrapper image and the CMD runs it with node -
# a CRLF checkout is harmless for node, but keep both files LF so the image
# is byte-stable across platforms and the file stays diff-friendly.
deploy/qm-pacgate/sandbox-local/** text eol=lf

# Deer-flow source patches: always LF, on every platform.
# Measured 2026-10-27 on a plain Windows clone (core.autocrlf=true): 19 of the
# 22 files under patches/ checked out as w/crlf. Python parses a CRLF copy fine
# (ast.parse OK, 698 CRLF markers), so the running stack was never broken - but
# two real costs followed. The worktree stops being byte-identical across
# machines (sha256 3E531976... here vs F7ADA451... in the source worktree), and
# `git am` cannot replay these commits: it aborts with "does not match index"
# on every file whose checkout was converted, which is the same CRLF trap
# recorded in plans/023-deer-flow-2.1-upgrade.md 2.1.
# These files are bind-mounted read-only into Linux containers, so LF is what
# the runtime wants anyway. Pinning it makes a clone, bundle and `git am`
# reproduce the same bytes on any platform.
deploy/client-bundle/patches/** text eol=lf
